    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d505-a1">

                <pb facs="0630" n="522" sameAs="frus:frus1893/pg522"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No. 512.[</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hicks to Señor
                            Jimenez.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Lima</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1893-06-14"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">June 14,
                    1893</hi>.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Minister</hi>: Referring to your excellency’s
                    note of June 9, 1893, in regard to the unfortunate affair at Mollendo on March
                    25, I am directed by my Government to accept the proposition made by your
                    excellency to pay to Enrique Meier the sum of <pb facs="0631" n="523"
                        xml:id="pg523"/> 2,000 sols in full payment of all claims for damages
                    arising from injury to the building in which was the consular agency of the
                    United States, as well as for the damages to the person and property of Mr.
                    Meier, the acting consular agent, growing out of the unfortunate affair before
                    mentioned.</p>
                <p>As I expect to close my official relations with Lima within a few days, it would
                    be extremely gratifying if the payment of the sum mentioned could be consummated
                    as soon as possible.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Hicks.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
